      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Ibuprofen 1600 mg four times daily comes to 6,400 mg/day, which is twice the labeled maximum for adults. The labeled maximum is 3,200 mg/day for prescription use, and 1,200 mg/day for over-the-counter use. A single 1,600 mg dose is also well above the usual 400\u2013800 mg per dose. At that level the risks of GI bleeding, kidney injury and cardiovascular events go up a lot, even in a patient with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nHere are some options within labeled limits:\n- **800 mg by mouth three times daily** (2,400 mg/day), which is a common dose for inflammatory conditions.\n- **800 mg by mouth four times daily** (3,200 mg/day), which is the labeled maximum.\n- **400\u2013600 mg by mouth every 6 hours as needed** for pain or fever.\n\nIf 1600 mg was meant to be a daily total, for example 800 mg twice daily, tell me and I can enter that.\n\nPlease tell me which regimen you want, and I'll enter it right away. Also let me know if you want a note on the order, such as \"take with food\"."
      }
